WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.110 --> 00:00:03.060
As we get closer and closer to the November
election.

00:00:03.060 --> 00:00:08.550
I've been talking about how much of Donald
Trump's behavior over the next three months

00:00:08.550 --> 00:00:15.339
is going to be coming of a place of desperation,
from a place of desperation, out of a sense

00:00:15.339 --> 00:00:16.900
of desperation.

00:00:16.900 --> 00:00:21.580
And David Shipler wrote a really interesting
article yesterday in Washington Monthly called

00:00:21.580 --> 00:00:26.960
Beware of a Cornered Trump, which really builds
on this idea that you and I have been talking

00:00:26.960 --> 00:00:31.670
about for a while, that if Donald Trump's
polling continues to be bad.

00:00:31.670 --> 00:00:35.800
And remember, he's pretending like he doesn't
believe the polling, but his actions speak

00:00:35.800 --> 00:00:41.390
otherwise, replacing his campaign manager
and all of that, you know, restarting corona

00:00:41.390 --> 00:00:44.860
virus briefings, all wearing a mask, all the
things that he's doing.

00:00:44.860 --> 00:00:48.260
If his polling doesn't improve, it doesn't
have to necessarily get worse.

00:00:48.260 --> 00:00:54.680
But just if it doesn't improve, we would expect,
based on everything we know about Donald Trump,

00:00:54.680 --> 00:01:01.040
that he would go even more in the directions
that we have seen him tend to directions of

00:01:01.040 --> 00:01:06.590
corruption and depravity and authoritarian
tendencies, which will likely become even

00:01:06.590 --> 00:01:07.590
more severe.

00:01:07.590 --> 00:01:09.070
And case in point.

00:01:09.070 --> 00:01:13.330
We're really already seeing that over the
last couple of weeks, the deployment of camouflaged

00:01:13.330 --> 00:01:18.130
troops with no badges to Portland, Oregon,
where they are throwing people into unmarked

00:01:18.130 --> 00:01:22.150
vans and claiming that they're going to expand
to more cities even as soon as this week.

00:01:22.150 --> 00:01:23.900
And we'll see if that happens.

00:01:23.900 --> 00:01:30.119
We're seeing the authoritarianism and really
the desperation and the disregard for human

00:01:30.119 --> 00:01:35.650
life manifest in the demand from Trump that
schools just open in the fall.

00:01:35.650 --> 00:01:37.580
Health considerations be damned.

00:01:37.580 --> 00:01:39.030
Just get open.

00:01:39.030 --> 00:01:46.560
We're seeing Donald Trump's desperation to
prevent people from voting against him manifest

00:01:46.560 --> 00:01:52.790
in his unhinged opposition to vote by mail,
which in practice this year just means expand

00:01:52.790 --> 00:01:54.740
absentee ballots through the process.

00:01:54.740 --> 00:02:00.299
We already have to whoever wants it, just
virulent opposition to that on completely

00:02:00.299 --> 00:02:01.910
false and bogus grounds.

00:02:01.910 --> 00:02:06.130
And as David Shipler says in this article,
which we're going to link to and I encourage

00:02:06.130 --> 00:02:10.569
you to read, and I like this term, Trump has
no moral breaks.

00:02:10.569 --> 00:02:14.410
There's nothing there where morality would
pump the brakes for him.

00:02:14.410 --> 00:02:19.150
David Shipler goes on to say his values are
those of a mafia boss who rewards and punishes

00:02:19.150 --> 00:02:26.020
those who protect or oppose him, who who protect
for opposing him, punishes those who protect

00:02:26.020 --> 00:02:27.080
or oppose him.

00:02:27.080 --> 00:02:32.840
Now, to be thorough, David Shipler also mentions
our fear could be wrong.

00:02:32.840 --> 00:02:36.379
Maybe Trump won't go completely off the rails,
for example.

00:02:36.379 --> 00:02:42.470
Maybe Trump won't send these armed paramilitaries
that are now being floated in places like

00:02:42.470 --> 00:02:43.470
Portland.

00:02:43.470 --> 00:02:48.260
Maybe Trump won't send them to monitor polling
places to intimidate voters in November.

00:02:48.260 --> 00:02:51.390
We're worried that he's going to do that,
but maybe he won't do it.

00:02:51.390 --> 00:02:56.970
Maybe our fear is overblown and we hope that
it's overblown in the sense that Trump could

00:02:56.970 --> 00:03:04.220
be too incompetent or unable to think far
enough ahead to actually do the horrible things

00:03:04.220 --> 00:03:06.480
that he would have no moral problem doing.

00:03:06.480 --> 00:03:10.349
If Trump stops short of what we fear he would
do.

00:03:10.349 --> 00:03:16.340
It would be not because of a moral awakening,
but because he forgets or is incompetent or

00:03:16.340 --> 00:03:18.470
is unable or unable to get something done.

00:03:18.470 --> 00:03:22.120
But there is this constant feedback loop of
vicious cycle.

00:03:22.120 --> 00:03:28.069
Trump's ignorance and delusions of grandeur
and narcissism reinforce his most dangerous

00:03:28.069 --> 00:03:35.230
impulses, which when he does and sees that
he gets a reaction, reinforces his narcissism

00:03:35.230 --> 00:03:39.290
and delusions of grandeur and viks it victimhood
mentality that no one's been treated as poorly

00:03:39.290 --> 00:03:40.290
as him.

00:03:40.290 --> 00:03:45.150
You combine this with this silver spoon upbringing
and what appears to be probably some personality

00:03:45.150 --> 00:03:49.210
disorders based on the mental health professionals
we've spoken to.

00:03:49.210 --> 00:03:51.680
There is no check on Trump's behavior anywhere.

00:03:51.680 --> 00:03:57.580
And in fact, when we hear that Trump had an
idea and didn't carry it out, it typically

00:03:57.580 --> 00:04:03.160
is because either, A, he gets distracted by
something else or B, a group of people in

00:04:03.160 --> 00:04:07.290
his in his administration are able to talk
him out of it or prevent him from doing it.

00:04:07.290 --> 00:04:09.060
And then he moves on to something else.

00:04:09.060 --> 00:04:13.290
It comes down to what can he get away with?

00:04:13.290 --> 00:04:17.289
What can the people around him stop him from
doing?

00:04:17.289 --> 00:04:23.940
And it also shouldn't be ignored that the
administration is in itself a threat by virtue

00:04:23.940 --> 00:04:25.520
of its mere existence.

00:04:25.520 --> 00:04:28.819
This is an administration that has been a
threat to the economy.

00:04:28.819 --> 00:04:33.279
It's been a threat to international relations
and our alliances with other countries.

00:04:33.279 --> 00:04:38.000
The administration, obviously, in what we're
seeing with coronavirus, has been an existential

00:04:38.000 --> 00:04:39.550
threat to public health.

00:04:39.550 --> 00:04:44.389
There continues to be a shockingly large percentage
of Americans, though, that still support the

00:04:44.389 --> 00:04:49.360
president and still support this administration,
despite everything that's going on right now.

00:04:49.360 --> 00:04:55.509
And that is sort of part two of how a desperate
Trump becomes a dangerous Trump.

00:04:55.509 --> 00:04:59.419
Some portion of Trump supporters, and I don't
know what.

00:04:59.419 --> 00:05:04.020
The number is, but I fear that it's a larger
percentage than we want to admit.

00:05:04.020 --> 00:05:08.789
Some portion of Trump supporters are willing
to do violence like real world violence, if

00:05:08.789 --> 00:05:15.589
that's what Donald Trump suggests or implies
or in any way signals may be appropriate.

00:05:15.589 --> 00:05:20.740
And so when Donald Trump said to Chris Wallace
on Sunday when asked, can you just say you'll

00:05:20.740 --> 00:05:23.240
accept the election results, Trump didn't
do it.

00:05:23.240 --> 00:05:27.059
He said, I have to see the election results
before I can tell you whether I would accept

00:05:27.059 --> 00:05:28.059
them.

00:05:28.059 --> 00:05:33.150
When you start to hear about the paramilitaries
showing up in Portland, we have to remember

00:05:33.150 --> 00:05:37.830
that a portion of this man's followers are
more than willing.

00:05:37.830 --> 00:05:42.309
Some are eager to get out there and commit
physical violence on the streets in the name

00:05:42.309 --> 00:05:43.919
of Donald Trump.

00:05:43.919 --> 00:05:51.080
Trump has shown us that if we try to predict
how far he will go, we're always wrong.

00:05:51.080 --> 00:05:56.830
He's always willing to go further than whatever
our predictions are at any point in time.

00:05:56.830 --> 00:06:01.910
And the more cornered he gets and that's what
I believe he increasingly is right now, the

00:06:01.910 --> 00:06:06.259
more outrageous and belligerent his behavior
is going to get.

00:06:06.259 --> 00:06:11.319
I wonder what stories there are to be told,
which maybe we will hear someday about the

00:06:11.319 --> 00:06:19.159
things Trump almost did during this administration
and someone was just barely able to but was

00:06:19.159 --> 00:06:21.849
able to stop him from doing it.

00:06:21.849 --> 00:06:25.169
You know, the stories about the things he
did are bad enough.

00:06:25.169 --> 00:06:31.860
There must be just a treasure trove of nightmares
about the things he almost did that someone

00:06:31.860 --> 00:06:33.309
stopped him from doing.

00:06:33.309 --> 00:06:38.099
And the next three plus months, three, three
months and a few weeks up until the election

00:06:38.099 --> 00:06:43.740
are likely to be the most dangerous Trump
because of the desperation and the feeling

00:06:43.740 --> 00:06:44.740
cornered.

00:06:44.740 --> 00:06:48.479
And the cognitive stuff is increasingly taking
center stage.

00:06:48.479 --> 00:08:16.219
And I want to talk about that a little bit
next.

